<section class="fcd-section" id="deploy-web">
    <h2>Deploying the website</h2>
    <p>GitHub Actions workflow <code>.github/workflows/deploy.yml</code>, triggered by a push to the branch <code>live</code>:</p>
    <ol class="fc-steps">
        <li><span class="fc-steps__title">Test</span><span><code>dotnet test --configuration Release</code> (there's no test project yet, so this only builds).</span></li>
        <li><span class="fc-steps__title">Build image</span><span>Docker build from <code>Dockerfile</code> (.NET 8, listens on port 8080) and push to <code>ghcr.io/&lt;owner&gt;/forest_churches:live</code>.</span></li>
        <li><span class="fc-steps__title">Deploy</span><span>Sign in to Azure and update Container App <code>forestchurches</code> in resource group <code>myResourceGroup</code> to the new image. A new revision starts; on start-up it applies database migrations and seeding.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="fcd-note fcd-note--warn">
        <ul>
            <li>The remote branch is named <code>Live</code> (capital L) but the workflow listens for <code>live</code>. GitHub branch filters are case-sensitive, so pushes to <code>Live</code> don't trigger it. Rename one to match.</li>
            <li>The Azure login step reads the repository secret <code>AZURE_CREDENTIALS</code> (service principal JSON). Create it before the first deployment of this version.</li>
            <li>Every image is tagged <code>live</code>, so there's no way to roll back by tag. Also tag with the commit SHA. In the meantime, roll back by re-activating the previous revision in Container Apps → Revisions.</li>
            <li>Migrations run automatically on start-up. A migration that fails is logged but the site still starts, possibly against an unexpected schema.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <p>To deploy the redesign: merge <code>redesign/forest-floor</code> into the deploy branch and push.</p>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="deploy-email">
    <h2>Deploying the email app</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Build: <code>dotnet publish -c Release</code>. Check the output contains <code>templates/*.html</code>.</li>
        <li>Upload the publish folder to the Plesk site for <code>api.forestchurches.co.uk</code> (Plesk file manager, Web Deploy or Git deployment), replacing the old files.</li>
        <li>Restart the application pool. The queue is in memory, so any emails waiting are lost: deploy just after a send run (check <code>queueLength = 0</code> on Email delivery).</li>
        <li>Open Site admin → Email delivery and confirm the app is healthy, then send a test (for example resend an invitation to yourself).</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="runbooks">
    <h2>Runbooks</h2>

    <h3>The site is down</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Check <code>https://forestchurches.co.uk/health</code>. 503 = database problem; no response = app not running.</li>
        <li>Azure Portal → Container App <code>forestchurches</code> → Revisions: is the latest revision running? Check <em>Log stream</em> for start-up exceptions.</li>
        <li>Start-up errors usually mean Key Vault access (expired <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code>), a missing secret, or the database refusing connections. See <a href="/docs/system/logging#startup">start-up failures</a>.</li>
        <li>If a new deployment broke it, activate the previous revision and route 100% of traffic to it.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Emails aren't arriving</h3>
    <p>Follow <a href="/docs/system/email#troubleshooting">EmailManagement troubleshooting</a>. Start at Site admin → Email delivery, find the email, then search its EmailId in Loki and Seq.</p>

    <h3>Add a site administrator</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Invite them (Site admin → Invitations) and let them register and confirm, or create them directly in Users → Create.</li>
        <li>Users → Edit → tick <strong>Admin</strong> (or SuperAdmin) → Save. They may need to sign out and in again for menus to update; permission checks apply immediately.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Someone is locked out of SuperAdmin</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>If they saw "This account has been locked out", wait 15 minutes (5 wrong attempts lock it). A SuperAdmin can unlock sooner by setting <code>LockoutEnd</code> to NULL and <code>AccessFailedCount</code> to 0 for that row in <code>AspNetUsers</code>.</li>
        <li>Use Forgot password on the sign-in page for that email.</li>
        <li>If email isn't working, another SuperAdmin can set them a role or delete and recreate the user.</li>
        <li>If no SuperAdmin can sign in: delete the seeded SuperAdmin's row from <code>AspNetUsers</code> (its church listing goes with it) and restart. The seeder recreates it from <code>sys-admin-username</code>/<code>-password</code>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Lost or corrupted Data Protection key ring</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Restore the key-ring blob from Blob soft delete or versioning if possible, and make sure the <code>data-key</code> key still exists in Key Vault (recover it from soft delete if not).</li>
        <li>If it can't be restored, delete the blob and restart: a new ring is created. Everyone must sign in again, and links in emails already sent stop working. Re-send outstanding invitations.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Rotate the Key Vault service principal secret</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>In Entra ID → App registrations → the app → Certificates &amp; secrets, add a new client secret.</li>
        <li>Update <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> in the Container App (creates a new revision) and on Plesk for the email app, then restart it.</li>
        <li>Check both apps start and send an email, then delete the old client secret.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>A church needs removing</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>To hide it temporarily, set its status to Closed (Site admin → Churches → Edit).</li>
        <li>To remove it, a SuperAdmin deletes the user in Users; the church listing and service times go with it. Then delete its events and its ChurchSuite credential row; see <a href="/docs/system/data#subject">data requests</a>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Clear out past events</h3>
    <p>Until clean-up is fixed (<a href="/docs/system/jobs#cleanup">Jobs</a>), use Site admin → Events → Past events, or in the database: <code>DELETE FROM Events WHERE Repeats = 'None' AND Date &lt; CURDATE() - INTERVAL 1 DAY;</code></p>

    <h3 id="rotate-exposed">Rotate the exposed secrets</h3>
    <p>These values were committed to Git, so treat them as known to anyone with a copy of the repository. Do this once the security fixes are deployed.</p>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Azure client secret</strong>: Entra ID → App registrations → the Key Vault app → Certificates &amp; secrets → <em>New client secret</em>. Put it in <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> on the Container App and on Plesk, restart both apps, then <strong>delete the old secret</strong>. Developers store theirs with <code>dotnet user-secrets</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Actions</strong>: create a service-principal JSON (<code>az ad sp create-for-rbac --sdk-auth</code>, scoped to the resource group) and save it as the repository secret <code>AZURE_CREDENTIALS</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>JWT key</strong>: generate a new random value (for example 64 characters from a password manager) and add it as a new version of <code>jwt-token-securityKey</code>. Restart the website and the email app together, then send a test email.</li>
        <li><strong>Google key</strong>: Google Cloud Console → APIs &amp; Services → Credentials → create a new key, restrict it to Geocoding API and Places API (and the site's outbound IP), save it as <code>google-api-key</code>, then delete the old key.</li>
        <li><strong>Development database password</strong>: change the password of the <code>database</code> user on the development MySQL server and update developers' user-secrets.</li>
        <li><strong>Purge history</strong>: with everyone's work pushed, run <code>git filter-repo</code> (or BFG) to remove <code>Properties/launchSettings.json</code> secret lines, <code>appsettings.Development.json</code> secrets, <code>DataProtectionKeys/</code>, <code>support/</code>, <code>wwwroot/js/map.js</code> and the email app's old <code>Program.cs</code> key from every branch, force-push, and have everyone re-clone. Rotation matters more than the purge: a purged secret may already have been copied.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="routine">
    <h2>Routine checks</h2>
    <div class="fcd-table-wrap">
        <table class="fcd-table">
            <thead><tr><th>How often</th><th>Check</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Weekly</td><td>Email delivery: any Failed? Logs/Loki: new error types? Past events and "Default Church" listings tidied?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Monthly</td><td>Invitations: delete expired rows. Users: remove people who've left. Google Cloud billing for Geocoding volume.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Quarterly</td><td>Purge old <code>applicationlogs</code>. Review SuperAdmin/Admin membership. Check NuGet packages for security updates.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Before expiry</td><td><code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> expiry date (Entra ID shows it); the domain and TLS certificates.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="issues">
    <h2>Known issues</h2>
    <p>Found while writing this documentation against <code>redesign/forest-floor</code> and <code>feature/delivery-status</code>, and updated after the October 2026 security fixes.</p>
    <h3>Fixed in October 2026</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> ChurchSuite connect/callback routes could sign the browser in as any user ID (account takeover).</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> Secrets removed from the repository files (rotation still needed, row 1 below).</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> Live log stream (<code>/logsHub</code>) open to anyone.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> Email app JWT key hardcoded; it now comes from Key Vault.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> ChurchSuite tokens and API keys stored in plain text.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> No account lockout; sign-in also skipped 2FA.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> No Content Security Policy.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> Google API key returned to any browser.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> User input inserted into email HTML unencoded.</li>
        <li><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--ok">Fixed</span> Open redirects after ChurchSuite; <code>/oauth-debug</code> in production.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Still open</h3>
    <div class="fcd-table-wrap">
        <table class="fcd-table">
            <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Severity</th><th>Issue</th><th>Where</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>1</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--danger">Critical</span></td><td>Secrets that were committed (Azure client secret, database password, Google key, email JWT key) still work and are in Git history.</td><td>Azure, Google Cloud, database host, Key Vault; Git history</td><td>Follow <a href="#rotate-exposed">Rotate the exposed secrets</a>, then purge history.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--warn">Medium</span></td><td>Event clean-up not scheduled and broken (null list, inverted date test).</td><td><code>EventContoller.cs</code>, <code>Program.cs</code></td><td>See <a href="/docs/system/jobs#cleanup">Jobs</a>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>3</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--warn">Medium</span></td><td>Email app <code>EmailScheduler</code> starts an extra endless loop every 5 minutes.</td><td>Email app <code>Classes/EmailScheduler.cs</code></td><td>Remove <code>EmailScheduler</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>4</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--warn">Medium</span></td><td>Email queue in memory: restart loses emails.</td><td>Email app <code>EmailController</code></td><td>Persist the queue (database table or Azure Queue).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>5</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--warn">Medium</span></td><td>Bulletin PDFs, Elmah and log files on non-persistent container disk.</td><td><code>wwwroot/uploads/bulletins</code>, <code>logs/</code></td><td>Mount Azure Files or use Blob Storage.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>6</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--warn">Medium</span></td><td>Deploy workflow listens for <code>live</code>, branch is <code>Live</code>.</td><td><code>deploy.yml</code></td><td>Match the names.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>7</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>No IP rate limiting on sign-in, the contact form or search (account lockout is on).</td><td><code>Program.cs</code></td><td>Add ASP.NET Core rate limiting.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>8</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Registration needs only a whitelisted address, not the token; whitelist match is case-sensitive.</td><td><code>Register.cshtml.cs</code></td><td>Require and validate the token on the register page; compare emails case-insensitively.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>9</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Email app Swagger public; SMTP may fall back to plain text.</td><td>Email app <code>appsettings.json</code>, <code>EmailSender.cs</code></td><td><code>EnableSwaggerInProduction=false</code>; <code>SecureSocketOptions.StartTls</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>10</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Contact us always shows Success even if the email failed.</td><td><code>Contact.cshtml.cs</code></td><td>Show the outcome from the hand-over.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>11</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Log search/download query columns that don't exist.</td><td><code>LogRetriver.cs</code></td><td>Use <code>LogLevel</code>/<code>MessageTemplate</code>; drop Url/Action.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>12</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>New and seeded churches go live immediately as "Default Church" with placeholder details.</td><td><code>Register.cshtml.cs</code>, <code>UsersController.SeedSuperAdminAsync</code></td><td>Create new listings as Closed until edited.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>13</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>"Bulletins" menu item shown to church users, who then get Access denied.</td><td>Site navigation</td><td>Show only with <code>Admin.Read</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>14</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Church search geocodes every church on every search.</td><td><code>NearMe.cshtml.cs</code></td><td>Store coordinates on the listing.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>15</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Deleting an account leaves events, ChurchSuite tokens and blobs.</td><td>Account deletion</td><td>Delete related data in the same operation.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>16</td><td><span class="fc-badge fc-badge--moss">Low</span></td><td>Seq secrets read but unused by the website; <code>/callback/{token}</code> and an unused postcode validator remain.</td><td>Various</td><td>Remove dead code and settings.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>The older HelpNDoc guides in <code>Docs/</code> describe automatic event clean-up and manual approval of new churches, which don't match the current code. This documentation replaces them.</p>
</section>
